fof_version: '0.1'
type: enemy
id: glassback_bull
name: Glassback Bull
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 0.1.0
enemy:
  tier: boss
  attack_modifier: 3
  defense_modifier: 1
  armor: light
  techniques:
  - ringing_charge
  special: RINGING CHARGE — when the bull closes from a distance, its antlers ring
    on impact and the note carries. Every glassback within a mile knows where the
    fight is, and the MM may bring one Glassback Cow to the edge of the scene at
    the end of the next exchange.
  description: Nine feet at the shoulder in season, and the rack is wider than a
    cart. The mineral has gone milky with age at the base and stayed clear at the
    tips, so that a bull in low sun looks like it is carrying a small sunrise on
    its head. It is not aggressive for eleven months of the year.
  disposition: In season, and therefore not reasonable. Out of season it is the
    single most avoidable danger in this book.
  first_target: The largest thing in the clearing. Armour makes you a candidate;
    standing still does not save you.
  triggers:
  - Charges in a straight line and cannot turn inside the charge — a character who
    commits to moving aside rather than meeting it is not in the path.
  - Rings the charge every time it closes from distance.
  morale: Breaks off at Resolve 2 and walks — not runs — back to the herd. Nothing
    in this book is less interested in finishing a fight.
  organization: One bull per herd, and only dangerous in the eight weeks of season.
  notes: 'TR breakdown: offense(+3 → 5) + durability(Resolve 6) + armor(light →
    1) + techniques(1) = 13. An entry-tier Boss, and one the party can decline.'
  negotiation: It wants distance and the herd behind it. Every step backwards buys
    real ground, and a party that gives it the clearing gets to keep everything
    else, including any antler already shed.
  resolve: 6
  phases:
  - resolve_threshold: 2
    description: The season goes out of it. The bull stops charging, turns broadside,
      and begins backing toward the herd. It will still answer anyone who closes,
      but it has stopped starting anything.
created_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00+00:00'
last_modified: '2026-08-02T00:00:00+00:00'
